  "id": "causal-attribution",
  "term": "causal attribution",
  "definition": "Causal attribution is the process of deciding whether a person’s psychological symptoms, injury, or impairment can reasonably be linked to a specific event. In forensic assessment, this judgment requires more than timing, plausibility, or diagnosis alone and depends on combining causal reasoning with consideration of the validity of the person’s reported and tested presentation.",
